sections.body:
Eight measures from the health check, each marked green, amber or red against the firm's own thresholds. Green is healthy, amber is worth watching, red needs action. Where the business was compared to its industry, each measure also says whether it sits below, within or above the middle half of businesses like it.

{{measures}}

That is everything. You have not been given the business's name, its industry, any figure, any document, or any account. That is deliberate: the advisor holds the detail and will add it when they edit your draft.

Return one JSON object and nothing else — no prose before it, no code fence around it.

{
  "readable": true,
  "document": { "name": "IR265 — General depreciation rates", "published": "2023-10", "country": "NZ" },
  "firstYearRuleFound": false,
  "rates": [
    { "category": "vehicles", "class": "Motor vehicles (transporting people, up to 12 seats)", "method": "dv", "dvRate": 0.5, "slRate": 0.4, "lifeYears": 4, "page": "61" }
  ],
  "classes": [
    { "class": "Engineering (heavy) — plant and machinery", "method": "dv", "dvRate": 0.13, "slRate": 0.085, "lifeYears": 15.5, "page": "9" }
  ],
  "unresolved": [
    { "class": "Right to use capacity in the Southern Cross Cable Network granted 7 Oct 2004 - 23 Nov 2006", "pages": "39, 40", "differs": "printed twice with different useful-life bands and different rates" }
  ],
  "whyUnreadable": null
}

readable — false if section 3 applies. When it is false, send an empty rates array and an empty classes array.
classes — every class the document publishes, as section 6 describes. Same fields as a rates entry, without a category.
unresolved — the entries you left out because you could not settle them, as section 3 describes. Empty where there were none. An entry here is NOT a rate: it names a class, the pages it appears on, and what differs, so a person can settle it against the document.
whyUnreadable — one plain sentence when readable is false, otherwise null.
document.country — the two-letter code for the authority that published this document, which may differ from the code you were given; say what the document is, not what was expected.
firstYearRuleFound — true only if this document describes a scheme letting a business deduct part of a new asset's cost in the year of purchase, over and above ordinary depreciation. Otherwise false.
method — "dv" where the schedule's ordinary basis is diminishing value, "sl" where it is straight line. The rate named by the method must be present.
slRate, lifeYears, page — use null where the document does not print them.

Return one JSON object and nothing else — no prose before it, no code fence around it.

{
  "readable": true,
  "classes": [
    { "class": "Engineering (heavy) — plant and machinery", "method": "dv", "dvRate": 0.13, "slRate": 0.085, "lifeYears": 15.5, "page": "9" }
  ],
  "unresolved": [
    { "class": "Right to use capacity in the Southern Cross Cable Network", "pages": "39, 40", "differs": "printed twice with different useful-life bands and different rates" }
  ],
  "whyUnreadable": null
}

readable — false if section 4 applies. When it is false, send an empty classes array.
classes — every class printed on your pages, in the order the document prints them. Empty only if your pages genuinely publish none, which is normal for a contents page or a chapter of prose.
method — "dv" where the schedule's ordinary basis is diminishing value, "sl" where it is straight line. The rate named by the method must be present.
slRate, lifeYears — use null where the document does not print them.
page — the page the class was printed on, as a string, within the range you were given.
unresolved — the entries you left out because you could not settle them, as section 6 describes. Empty where there were none.
whyUnreadable — one plain sentence when readable is false, otherwise null.

You have been given DOCUMENT NAMES ONLY. Not their contents, not a summary of them, not an extract. No document has been read by anything, and none will be.

The eight points:

{{points}}

The document names:

{{documents}}

Nothing else exists for this task. No client, no person, no meeting and no transcript is described anywhere in this request, and you must never ask for one or assume one.

Return one JSON object and nothing else — no prose before it, no code fence around it.

{
  "points": [
    { "id": "lawful-recording", "covered": true, "coveredBy": ["Legal opinion — Harrow & Tait"] },
    { "id": "ipp3a", "covered": false, "coveredBy": [] }
  ]
}

points — one entry for every point you were given, in the order you were given them, using the id exactly as it was written.
covered — true only where a named document plainly addresses that point.
coveredBy — the names of the documents that do, copied exactly as they were given to you. Empty when covered is false.
